# No hardcoding (locked)

**Hardcoding is a bug.** Applies to `packages/**` and `example/**` (debug shell included).

## Copy (i18n)
- All user-visible strings via `t(key)` / `LocaleService.t` / `LocaleKeys.*`.
- Includes: buttons, titles, tips, toasts, validation, placeholders, `title` / `aria-label`, stub checklists, nav labels.
- Add key to **every** locale pack (`zh-CN` · `zh-TW` · `en-US` · `ja-JP` · `ko-KR` · `ko-KP` · `ru-RU` · `ar-SA`). Missing key = bug / compile fail.
- Route `meta.title` Chinese/hardcoded fallbacks are forbidden as primary source — use `meta.titleKey` only; fallback may be the key string.
- Mock **data values** may be Latin sample names/emails; **role/status labels** shown in UI must be codes + `t()`, never locale-bound literals as display text.
- Brand / product proper nouns (`AMG-WebUI`) may stay literal once; comment `/* brand */` if needed.

## Visual tokens
- No raw hex / rgb / hardcoded `px`/`rem` for color, spacing, radius, type, shadow in component/page CSS.
- Consume `--ds-*` · `--surface-*` · `--text-*` · `--theme-*` · `--spacing-*` · `--font-size-*` · `--border-radius-*` · `--shadow-*` · `--height-*`.
- Exception: `0`, `1px` hairlines, `100%` / `auto` / unitless flex ratios.

## Don’t
- Chinese/English literals in SFC templates or Toast `summary`/`detail`.
- `style="color:#…"` / SCSS `#hex` except inside official theme pack primitives.
- Invent ad-hoc CSS vars or skip updating locale packs / TOKENS when adding UI copy or scale values.

Docs: `packages/locale/I18N.md` · `packages/theme/TOKENS.md` · `AGENTS.md`
